# Real installed users' sudo access. shellprocess.conf strips
# sudoers.d/liveuser (a live-medium-only NOPASSWD-for-all-wheel
# convenience) during install specifically because leaving it in place
# would silently grant the new real account passwordless root -- but
# that cleanup never left wheel members with ANY sudo rule at all,
# which is just as wrong the other way (a normal installed user
# couldn't sudo, period). This is the real, password-required rule
# that's meant to actually ship: not removed by the liveuser cleanup
# above since it targets a different filename.
%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL
